msgid "Resolving mongo+srv:// URLs"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When using `mongo+srv://` URLs, the MongoDB driver resolves DNS SRV records "
"to retrieve the list of hosts to connect to.\n"
"By default, it relies on a DNS client implemented using JNDI."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For security reasons, Quarkus restricts JNDI usage within applications to "
"help mitigate potential vulnerabilities like Log4Shell.\n"
"To support `mongo+srv://`, Quarkus provides an alternative DNS client."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"However, in some environments, this alternative DNS client may be unable to "
"resolve `SRV` records.\n"
"If you encounter such issues, you can revert to the MongoDB driver’s default "
"DNS client by setting the following properties:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This restores the default JNDI-based resolution mechanism used by the "
"MongoDB driver."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use the MongoDB Dev Services"
msgstr ""

msgid "See xref:mongodb-dev-services.adoc[MongoDB Dev Services]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Multiple MongoDB Clients"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"MongoDB allows you to configure multiple clients.\n"
"Using several clients works the same way as having a single client."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Notice there's an extra bit in the key (the `users` and `inventory` "
"segments).\n"
"The syntax is as follows: `quarkus.mongodb.[optional name.][mongo connection "
"property]`.\n"
"If the name is omitted, it configures the default client."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The use of multiple MongoDB clients enables multi-tenancy for MongoDB by "
"allowing to connect to multiple MongoDB clusters. +\n"
"If you want to connect to multiple databases inside the same cluster,\n"
"multiple clients are **not** necessary as a single client is able to access "
"all databases in the same cluster\n"
"(as a JDBC connection is able to access to multiple schemas inside the same "
"database)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Named Mongo client Injection"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When using multiple clients, each `MongoClient`, you can select the client "
"to inject using the `io.quarkus.mongodb.MongoClientName` qualifier.\n"
"Using the above properties to configure three different clients, you can "
"also inject each one as follows:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Activate or deactivate Mongo Clients"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a Mongo Client is configured at build time, and its URL is set at "
"runtime, it is active by default. Quarkus\n"
"starts the corresponding Mongo Client when the application starts."
msgstr ""

msgid "To deactivate a Mongo Client at runtime, either:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Do not set `quarkus.mongodb[.optional name].hosts` or `quarkus.mongodb[."
"optional name].connection-#string#`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Set `quarkus.mongodb[.optional name].active` to `false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "If a Mongo Client is not active:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Mongo Client does not attempt to connect to Mongo during application "
"startup."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Mongo Client does not contribute a <<mongo-health-check,health check>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Static CDI injection points involving the Mongo Client, such as `@Inject "
"ReactiveMongoClient mongoClient` or `@Inject MongoClient mongoClient`, cause "
"application startup to fail."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dynamic retrieval of the Mongo Client, such as through `CDI."
"getBeanContainer()`, `Arc.instance()`, or an injected "
"`Instance<ReactiveMongoClient>`, causes an exception to be thrown."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Other Quarkus extensions that consume the Mongo Client may cause application "
"startup to fail."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This feature is especially useful when the application must dynamically "
"select a Mongo Client from a predefined set at\n"
"runtime."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Setting `quarkus.mongodb.one.active=true` xref:config-reference."
"adoc#configuration-sources[at runtime] makes only the\n"
"Mongo Client `one` available.\n"
"Setting `quarkus.mongodb.two.active=true` at runtime makes only the Mongo "
"Client `two` available."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A Mongo Client (either default or named) must always be discoverable at "
"build-time to be considered for runtime\n"
"injection. This can be done by injecting the Mongo Client name with "
"`@MongoClientName`. If the Mongo Client name may be\n"
"active or inactive, it needs to use the wrapper `InjectableInstance<>`, or "
"else Quarkus will throw an exception at\n"
"startup time if the Mongo Client is inactive. Alternatively, Mongo Clients "
"may also be discovered via configuration."
msgstr ""

